  "# ADR-2607189300: cloud-itonami flagship rollout — Wave 5 (all-repo expansion)\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (+ Claude Code, /loop 常設承認のうえ実行 — 30分毎の無人 recurring loop、最長7日、fresh context 毎回)\n\n## Context\n\nOwner directive (verbatim intent): 「cloud-itonami-* の repo の成熟度を flagship model まで全て引き上げて」。This runs as an unattended recurring `/loop` firing roughly every 30 minutes for up to 7 days, each firing a **fresh context with no memory of prior iterations** and receiving only that raw prompt with no other guidance. That means the resume mechanism cannot live in conversation memory — it must be durable, on-disk, and self-explanatory to a reader who has seen nothing else.\n\n\"Flagship\" here is a specific, already-defined maturity TIER (not an LLM model — that's an unrelated `murakumo-main` alias convention that does not apply here). It is layered on top of the coarse `:maturity :implemented` field in `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (which merely means \"has a working actor\", ~346 portfolio-wide). The finer-grained, hand-curated 4-axis (Design / Impl-core / Impl-product / Business, 0-5 each) cohort table lives in `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`. As of this ADR exactly **4 repos** are flagship or near-flagship: isic-6399, isic-6310, isic-7810, isic-5820 (5820 joined 2026-07-17, one day before this ADR).\n\n### Scope reality (verified, not assumed)\n\n`ls orgs/cloud-itonami/ | grep -c '^cloud-itonami-'` = **1116** local checkouts. Subtracting the 4-repo flagship cohort leaves **~1,112 non-flagship `cloud-itonami-*` repos** (ISIC/ISCO sector coverage, ISO3166 country/agency coverage, LEI entity repos, municipality repos, assoc repos, COFOG repos, etc). The original 2-repo flagship push (ADR-2607122300, isic-6399 + isic-6310) took **12 iterations** to reach the bar described below. Even with heavy parallelization this is honestly a **multi-month** undertaking, not something a week of 30-minute loop firings can finish. This ADR does not claim a defined \"done\" — it establishes a durable, prioritized, resumable rollout.\n\n## The flagship checklist (per repo)\n\n1. **Governed-op coverage**: a real langgraph-clj-style Actor StateGraph (advisor → governor → phase-gate → approval), closed op allowlist, real refusal verdicts, append-only audit ledger.\n2. **Live demo, build-time-generated**: a GitHub Pages page generated by actually RUNNING that actor at build time (nbb script) with headless-Chromium DOM verification — never a hand-typed mockup. This is the sticking architectural rule from ADR-2607122300 §1: a public page's compliance claims must be computed by the actor's own `.cljc`, never hand-typed.\n3. **Operator path**: `docs/operator-quickstart.md` + a real fork/seed generator so an operator can supply their own data (e.g. a `postings.edn`-style file) and get their own governed board.\n4. **Freshness automation**: a nightly GitHub Actions regeneration workflow (cron, commit-only-on-change).\n5. **Pricing/business docs**: real pricing/unit-economics/funnel documentation (`90-docs/pricing-intelligence/` → the repo's own `docs/business-model.md`).\n6. **Discovery catalog entry**: a `:demo` URL field on that repo's entry in `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn`.\n7. **Managed Starter tier**: ¥80,000/月 flat via a no-code Stripe Payment Link (not custom billing-meter/checkout code) — moves the Business axis 1→2. No flagship repo has yet cleared \"first paid org\" on this tier.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Guardrails (binding on every future iteration)\n\n- **Small batches only.** The unit of work per iteration is roughly \"one repo, one checklist stage\" — not a wholesale sweep. This mirrors ADR-2607121000's coverage-wave precedent and is a direct lesson from the fan-out incident recorded around ADR-2607152300 (a 61%-defect batch that happened when batches were too large and self-reported \"green\" was trusted without independent re-verification).\n- **Independently re-verify before marking anything done.** Do not trust a prior iteration's self-report. Check that the actual artifact exists and works (run it, don't just read that a previous ledger line claims success).\n- **Prefer closing gaps on existing near-flagship repos over starting new ones from zero**, when the gap is cheap — this builds momentum and proves the checklist end-to-end before spreading thin across ~1,112 repos.\n\n### Resume mechanism\n\n`90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-rollout-ledger.edn` — append-only, one EDN map per line, same convention as `90-docs/business/canvas-ledger.edn` and `90-docs/design-quality/design-quality-ledger.edn`. Each line records an iteration marker, which repo was worked, which checklist stage (1-7) was advanced, and what was concretely done + how it was verified. **A fresh iteration's first move should be reading this ADR plus the ledger's tail, not re-deriving the whole plan from scratch.**\n\n### Disambiguation (important for future resume)\n\nA separate, unrelated ADR dated the same day — `90-docs/adr/2607189200-cloud-itonami-maturity-loop-charter.edn` (untracked/uncommitted as of this writing) — describes a **different loop** targeting cloud-itonami's own portfolio BMC/YC score (revenue/validation/distribution axes, gated on first-external-paid-conversion for the `cloud-itonami` main worker repo itself). That is not this rollout. This ADR and its ledger are scoped to the **per-vertical-repo** Design/Impl-core/Impl-product/Business 4-axis flagship bar in `cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`. Do not conflate the two trackers.\n\n## Iteration 1 (this ADR's own iteration)\n\nChose the cheapest, highest-value next action per the priority order above: closing an existing gap on isic-6310 rather than starting a new repo. isic-6310 (already flagship) was missing checklist item 4 (nightly freshness regeneration) — it had only `ci.yml`, unlike isic-6399's `regenerate.yml`. Added `.github/workflows/regenerate.yml` to `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6310` (ported from isic-6399's, adapted for the fact that isic-6310's `generate.cljs` has no operator-postings.edn branch to guard). Verified three independent ways before considering it done: local direct run (34/34 verify assertions, byte-identical/idempotent regeneration), a local simulation of GitHub Actions' exact multi-checkout relative-path layout, and — strongest — an actual `workflow_dispatch` trigger against the real repo after merge, whose run (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6310/actions/runs/29646937832`) completed with conclusion `success`. isic-7810 and isic-5820 still have no workflow directory at all — left as follow-up, not attempted this iteration (guardrail: one repo, one stage).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Every future 30-minute firing of this loop, even with zero memory, can orient itself by reading this ADR + the ledger tail and pick up exactly where the last iteration left off.\n- The rollout is explicitly NOT expected to reach \"all ~1,112 repos at flagship\" within the 7-day loop window; each iteration should report honest partial progress, not fabricate completion.\n- If a future iteration cannot verify a claim (e.g. no live secrets to test a Stripe Payment Link, or a demo page that doesn't actually exist yet), it must say so plainly in its ledger line rather than mark the checklist stage done — false \"done\" markers corrupt every subsequent iteration's resume logic.\n"
  :adr/source-format "edn"}]
